NEARS-2168 QA — task_bug evidence: kill-time pgid check false-aborts on siblings' own paths

Repro (live, 2026-08-22):
Two real `flutter test` runs launched concurrently in different worktrees
(nears-NEARS-2338-payment-cart-checkdot = still running, nears-NEARS-2347-cover-caption-ar =
target). Target worktree's flutter_tools launcher (pid 39857) SIGKILLed while it had 5 live
flutter_tester workers (41305,41471,41472,41514,41596), all sharing pgid 39852, all
genuinely orphaned (ppid 1, no live flutter_tools/dart-test ancestor, cwd confirmed under
the target worktree) -- exactly the scenario flutter-tester-reap.sh is meant to reap.

Real (non-dry-run) invocation:
  bash scripts/newtask-guards/flutter-tester-reap.sh --worktree /Users/Apple/Projects/nears-NEARS-2347-cover-caption-ar

Output:
  CANDIDATE pid 41305 -- flutter_tester, no live flutter_tools/dart test ancestor (ppid=1 stat=SN)
    ABORT pid 41305 -- a live dart/dartaotruntime process shares its process group (39852)
  CANDIDATE pid 41471 -- flutter_tester, no live flutter_tools/dart test ancestor (ppid=1 stat=SN)
    ABORT pid 41471 -- a live dart/dartaotruntime process shares its process group (39852)
  CANDIDATE pid 41472 -- flutter_tester, no live flutter_tools/dart test ancestor (ppid=1 stat=SN)
    ABORT pid 41472 -- a live dart/dartaotruntime process shares its process group (39852)
  CANDIDATE pid 41514 -- flutter_tester, no live flutter_tools/dart test ancestor (ppid=1 stat=SN)
    ABORT pid 41514 -- a live dart/dartaotruntime process shares its process group (39852)
  CANDIDATE pid 41596 -- flutter_tester, no live flutter_tools/dart test ancestor (ppid=1 stat=SN)
    ABORT pid 41596 -- a live dart/dartaotruntime process shares its process group (39852)
  == examined:5 killed:0 skipped:0 aborted:5 ==

Root cause (flutter-tester-reap.sh:230-234, _ftr_reverify_and_kill):
  pgid="$(ps -o pgid= -p "$pid" ...)"
  ps -axeo pid=,pgid=,args= | awk -v g="$pgid" -v me="$pid" '$1!=me && $2==g' | grep -qiE 'dart|dartaotruntime'

This is a raw substring grep over the full `args=` text of every OTHER process sharing the
pgid, not a check of any process's binary/name. Every flutter_tester's own command line
contains the literal substring "dart" from its own file paths
(--packages=.../.dart_tool/package_config.json and .../listener.dart.dill) -- confirmed live:

  $ ps -axeo pid=,pgid=,args= | awk -v g=39852 -v me=41305 '$1!=me && $2==g' | grep -oiE 'dart[a-z]*'
  dart
  dart
  dart
  dart
  dart
  dart
  dart
  dart
  dart
  dart
  dart
  dart

So ANY time a `flutter test` run leaves 2+ flutter_tester workers orphaned together in one
process group -- the normal/expected shape for a parallel test run, and exactly the shape
the script's OWN header/corroboration comments cite as the motivating real-world case
("measured live: 7, NEARS-2057-module-reload") -- the kill-time gate false-aborts every one
of them on sight of its own siblings' paths, never an actual live dart/dartaotruntime
process. Confirmed (read-only, untouched) that NEARS-2057-module-reload's 7 pre-existing
orphans share pgid 83127 -- the identical shape -- so they would hit this same false-abort
if ever targeted.

Impact: AC3 explicitly requires "(a) the completed run's flutter_tester is killed" under a
real non-dry-run scoped invocation. Demonstrated live: killed:0, aborted:5. The reaper's
kill-time safety net, as implemented, cannot reap the realistic multi-worker-orphan case at
all -- it only succeeds when a SOLE flutter_tester is left alone in its own pgid.

Scope isolation (the other half of AC3) worked correctly: WT-B's live launcher/workers
(pid 32716 + children) were never examined by the WT-A-scoped run (examined:5, all WT-A
pids) -- confirming --worktree scoping itself is sound; only the kill-time gate is broken.
